  "source": "https://arxiv.org/html/1509.00149",
  "algorithm": "At a nonterminal decision successor, update the selected bandits with its cumulative raw-return mean after the current simulation. Propagate and accumulate the raw terminal return. Terminal and Bernoulli chance outcomes remain unaveraged. The four arms cross UCB/Exp3-IX selection with raw/child-mean updates, using the same seed list and simulation checkpoints.",
  "decision": "Do not add averaging alone to UCB: its whole-policy gap increases in this model. Exp3-IX with child-mean updates merits a separate native-game experiment; this model does not establish a bot improvement, a finite-budget guarantee or a general convergence theorem.",
  "scope": "An abstract waiting-chain game with two row actions, three column actions and seven decision stages. The continue/continue pair advances one stage; other pairs terminate with payoff p or zero. p=0.91461181640625 and the resulting matrices agree with the archived Bond continuation intervals. Collapsed off-chain subgames grant optimal continuation; the actual engine, hidden information, rollouts and state abstraction are absent. The stochastic control uses a Bernoulli(p) terminal payoff. All nodes are available from the start. Exact rational backward best responses evaluate both players\u2019 empirical behavioral policies over the entire abstract game. Gap is the sum of their value losses, not a single-player loss or the complete real-game exploitability. Default bot code is unchanged."
}
